# Signal engine (`engine/`, `test/`)

- Every libsignal call that reads or writes protocol records goes through `engine/protocol/protocol.ts`, which hydrates a `ProtocolStore`, makes one call, flushes changes, and holds a lock throughout. Don't call `libsignal.*` session/identity APIs elsewhere.
- Match libsignal failures by `errorCode(err)` (`UntrustedIdentity`, `DuplicatedMessage`, ...), not by message text.
- Incoming envelopes decrypt one at a time via `SignalClient.enqueueDecryptEnvelope` (`net/client.ts`).
- Layout: `protocol/` (libsignal, store, PreKeys), `net/` (`http.ts` hosts and HTTP types, `proto.ts`, `provisioning.ts`, `receive.ts`, `client.ts`), `services/` (Storage Service, profiles, Groups V2), `crypto/`.

## Protobuf (protobuf-es v2)

- Build messages with `create(Schema, init)`, encode with `toBinary`, decode with `fromBinary`. Use `MessageInitShape<typeof XSchema>` for init types.
- Never spread a generated message: unset proto2 fields live on the prototype and are lost.

```ts
// Bad: drops prototype defaults such as `key`
const copy = { ...pointer, fileName };
// Good
const copy = create(AttachmentPointerSchema, { key: pointer.key, digest: pointer.digest, fileName });
```

- uint64 fields are `bigint` (use `num()`), oneofs are `{ case, value }`, and proto2 fields default to empty values, not `undefined`.
- Never edit `engine/gen/`; regenerate with `npm run gen:protos`.

## Trust and input

- Recipients are ACIs (`isAci`); resolve phone numbers through synced contacts.
- Accept sync messages only when the envelope source is our own ACI.
- Treat frames, protobufs, and HTTP responses as untrusted; validate lengths and types before use.
- Compare MACs and secrets with `constantTimeEqual`.

## Tests

- Interop tests in `test/interop.test.ts` must keep passing against `@signalapp/libsignal-client` at the pinned version; add a both-directions case when wrapping new libsignal functionality.
- `test/support.ts` loads the wasm module from `app/vendor/`, so run `npm run build:wasm` first.
